From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 998: default the bSTA priority lookup like its siblings

mapagent_disable_lower_bk() reads a bsta sections priority without a default
and then uses it in an arithmetic comparison. Any bsta section without an
explicit priority makes the shell abort the test with

  mapagent[...]: sh: out of range

That this is an oversight rather than intent is visible in the same file: the
other two priority lookups, at lines 862 and 1226, both pass "2".

Such sections do occur in practice. On a node running an MLD backhaul a
bsta wlan0 section reappears after every removal, generated without a
priority, and the message then repeats for every uplink event.

Verified on hardware 2026-07-28: with the default in place the message stops
immediately. Note this does not by itself keep the agent alive -- the crash
loop it appears alongside has a different cause, see patch 997 -- so it is
easy to mistake this for the fault. It is a separate, real defect.

--- a/src/script/multiap
+++ b/src/script/multiap
@@ -1261,7 +1261,7 @@
 		local enabled="1"
 
 		config_get ifname $1 ifname
-		config_get priority $1 priority
+		config_get priority $1 priority "2"
 
 		[ "$ifname" != "$2" -a "$priority" -gt "$3" ] && enabled="0"
 
